{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfhTsq7fVxFPrdhJffVq3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"sections\":[{\"sid\":\"SEC023\",\"paras\":[{\"h\":\"p1\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Read John chapter 17 again, because everything Jesus does there flows out of one fact: he could not do anything apart from the Father. He said, \\\"I live because of the living Father.\\\" His life and his ministry rested entirely on that union, and it is out of that dependence that he prays, \\\"so that they can be one like us.\\\" That is an inference drawn from the text, and it is a legitimate one: he is not simply praying for cooperation among believers, he is praying for union with himself and the Father.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA078\",\"SRC002396\",\"SRC002405\",\"SRC002411\"]},{\"h\":\"p2\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"When people hear Jesus pray for unity, they often assume he means institutional unity among churches. But he was not particularly praying about that. What he was praying for was union with him, union with God himself. The oneness in view is not primarily an arrangement between believers and other believers; it is each believer's union with God.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA079\",\"SRC002400\",\"SRC002403\",\"SRC002404\"]},{\"h\":\"p3\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Notice also what he does not ask for. \\\"I do not ask you to take them from the world, but to preserve them from evil.\\\" He does not pray for an exit; he prays for protection while his own remain in the world, not of it, just as he himself was not of the world.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA080\",\"SRC002434\",\"SRC002436\",\"SRC002437\",\"SRC002438\"]},{\"h\":\"p4\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Jesus says, \\\"Your word is the truth,\\\" and then, \\\"I sanctify myself for them, so that they too may be sanctified by the truth.\\\" His own setting-apart becomes the ground on which their sanctification rests, and the instrument of that sanctification is God's word, given to them plainly, as he says, \\\"Give them your raw word.\\\"\",\"e\":[\"IDEA089\",\"SRC002557\",\"SRC002558\",\"SRC002570\",\"SRC002571\",\"SRC002572\"]},{\"h\":\"p5\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"And the prayer does not stop with the disciples standing in front of him. \\\"It is not only for them that I pray, but also for those who will believe in me by their word.\\\" That reaches across every generation since, including ours.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA090\",\"SRC002573\",\"SRC002574\",\"SRC002575\"]}]},{\"sid\":\"SEC024\",\"paras\":[{\"h\":\"p6\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"The unity he prays for has a specific shape: \\\"so that all may be one like you, Father. You are in me, and as I am in you, so that they too may be one in us.\\\" This is not a looser kind of agreement; it is the same kind of mutual indwelling that exists between the Father and the Son, now extended to believers.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA091\",\"SRC002576\",\"SRC002577\",\"SRC002578\",\"SRC002579\",\"SRC002580\"]},{\"h\":\"p7\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Jesus states the purpose directly: \\\"For the world to believe that you sent me, I have given them the glory... when they are one as we are one... when they are perfectly one, the world knows that you had sent me and that you have loved them as you have loved me.\\\" The world's belief is tied to that perfect oneness, and that same oneness becomes evidence to the world of the Father's love for believers.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA092\",\"SRC002589\",\"SRC002597\",\"SRC002598\",\"SRC002602\",\"SRC002604\",\"SRC002605\",\"SRC002606\"]},{\"h\":\"p8\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"He says plainly, \\\"I have given them the glory,\\\" at the same level as Jesus Christ himself. That is a staggering statement, and it should not be handled lightly or assumed to be understood just because the words are familiar.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA093\",\"SRC002590\",\"SRC002593\",\"SRC002626\",\"SRC002627\",\"SRC002628\",\"SRC002629\"]},{\"h\":\"p9\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"So the question is not first of all a theological definition of glory. The question is, where is the glory? Maybe the real question each of us has to ask is not \\\"what is glory\\\" in the abstract, but what glory is for you, personally. Is it in your life? Est-ce que c'est dans ta vie?\",\"e\":[\"IDEA094\",\"SRC002651\",\"SRC002652\",\"SRC002670\",\"SRC002672\",\"SRC002677\",\"SRC002685\",\"SRC002686\"]}]},{\"sid\":\"SEC025\",\"paras\":[{\"h\":\"p10\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Tu sais quand une enfant de Dieu aujourd'hui te dit, you know when a child of God tells you today that they \\\"receive by faith,\\\" ça veut dire qu'il n'a pas ça — that means they do not have it. Not that they have not received it; they have received it, but they do not yet have it in experience. C'est quelque part qu'on ne voit pas — it is somewhere not yet seen. Pour voir ça, il faut voir dans la foi, il faut voir par la foi. To see that, you have to see through faith.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA095\",\"SRC002689\",\"SRC002691\",\"SRC002693\",\"SRC002695\",\"SRC002696\",\"SRC002698\",\"SRC002699\",\"SRC002700\"]},{\"h\":\"p11\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"And you don't have taxi money to go today, but — je suis un zillionnaire, \\\"I am a zillionaire.\\\" There is a place of humble beginning. But be factual with your walk with God. God wants to give you his experience, not merely a confession detached from what is actually true of your life right now.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA096\",\"SRC002710\",\"SRC002714\",\"SRC002717\",\"SRC002719\",\"SRC002721\"]},{\"h\":\"p12\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"In the days of your infancy — what the word calls the days of ignorance — God will overlook. But a time will come when a commandment comes upon your life. You know the days when you are a baby; Galatians chapter 4 says that until the appointed time, you are not different from a slave, even though you are heir of all. Growth brings greater responsibility; what was once overlooked becomes something you are now accountable for. Read Acts 17.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA097\",\"SRC002728\",\"SRC002731\",\"SRC002733\",\"SRC002735\",\"SRC002737\",\"SRC002744\",\"SRC002746\",\"SRC002750\",\"SRC002752\"],\"u\":[]}]},{\"sid\":\"SEC026\",\"paras\":[{\"h\":\"p13\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"He did not commission us to prepare for his second coming. He did not send us simply to get ready for that day. \\\"Blessed is the servant whose master will find doing his job when he comes.\\\" Just be doing what you're supposed to be doing.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA081\",\"SRC002466\",\"SRC002467\",\"SRC002477\",\"SRC002478\",\"SRC002480\"]},{\"h\":\"p14\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Don't occupy yourself with the time when everything will end. Just be busy serving God. If you're serving him, and your relationship with him is well, that is what matters.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA082\",\"SRC002481\",\"SRC002482\",\"SRC002485\",\"SRC002486\",\"SRC002487\"]},{\"h\":\"p15\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"If he comes and he wants to rapture, let him rapture. And if he doesn't come for rapture, he comes a second time — let him come for a second time. Either way is not the believer's concern; the priority is a right relationship with God.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA083\",\"SRC002488\",\"SRC002489\",\"SRC002492\",\"SRC002493\",\"SRC002494\"]},{\"h\":\"p16\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"The doctrine of rapture, preached the way it so often is, is creating a lethargic Christianity. You understand what I mean by that? A church waiting to be taken out produces passive people rather than active disciples.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA084\",\"SRC002495\",\"SRC002496\"]},{\"h\":\"p17\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Read the second Peter chapter 3. Peter addressed scoffers who thought God's promises were delayed. He said, let me tell you this truth: one day and a thousand years don't make any difference before God. God is not like man. He's not under pressure.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA085\",\"SRC002512\",\"SRC002522\",\"SRC002525\",\"SRC002526\",\"SRC002527\",\"SRC002528\"],\"u\":[]},{\"h\":\"p18\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Two thousand years later, we're still behaving the same way. Picture that. The impatience Peter rebuked is the same impatience the church still carries today.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA086\",\"SRC002531\",\"SRC002532\",\"SRC002533\"]},{\"h\":\"p19\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"All of you who are thinking, I have to preach the second coming of Jesus, I have to preach the rapture — you're not impressing anybody. Preach Christ. Preach Christ. Christ is here now. I say he is here now.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA087\",\"SRC002538\",\"SRC002539\",\"SRC002540\",\"SRC002541\",\"SRC002542\",\"SRC002543\",\"SRC002544\",\"SRC002545\"]},{\"h\":\"p20\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"In fact, he's coming for people who are in him. Take people to Christ. Present union with him matters more than debates about timing. Read Acts 17.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA088\",\"SRC002546\",\"SRC002547\",\"SRC002548\",\"SRC002739\",\"SRC002741\"]}]},{\"sid\":\"SEC027\",\"paras\":[{\"h\":\"p21\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Out of the abundance, of the abundance of your communion with the Father, we flow. These things we are talking about will overflow — not because we rehearsed them, but because communion with the Father produces them naturally.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA105\",\"SRC002938\",\"SRC002939\",\"SRC002941\",\"SRC002942\",\"SRC002943\",\"SRC002944\",\"SRC002945\"]},{\"h\":\"p22\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"They must be conscious. Someone can kneel down and begin to pray, and then add scripture to it — \\\"let your enemies be scattered\\\" — we know that is scripture prayer, but you have prayed nothing. Reciting a borrowed phrase, however biblical in its origin, is not the same as praying out of real union and presence-consciousness, and it produces no manifestation.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA106\",\"EX016\",\"SRC002966\",\"SRC002971\",\"SRC002972\",\"SRC002973\",\"SRC002974\",\"SRC002976\",\"SRC002977\",\"SRC002978\"]},{\"h\":\"p23\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Where is he supposed to arise from? He must rise from where? He comes from where? He comes — you are the temple. From where he comes, you brought him here. You are his house. His holiness is here. The Holy Spirit does not need to be summoned from a distance, because he already dwells in the believer as his temple and his house.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA107\",\"SRC002980\",\"SRC002981\",\"SRC002986\",\"SRC002987\",\"SRC003005\",\"SRC003006\",\"SRC003007\",\"SRC003008\",\"SRC003009\"]},{\"h\":\"p24\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Because we carry God, of course when we carry God it's easy for us to unite, because birds of the same faith have flocked together. You will never know tribe anymore. We will never know clan if we are all in the Holy Ghost. Neither male or female becomes real; Jew or Greek become real distinctions when believers live in conscious union and carry God's presence — those divisions dissolve.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA108\",\"SRC003023\",\"SRC003024\",\"SRC003025\",\"SRC003026\",\"SRC003027\",\"SRC003031\",\"SRC003037\",\"SRC003039\",\"SRC003044\",\"SRC003045\"]}]},{\"sid\":\"SEC028\",\"paras\":[{\"h\":\"p25\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"We have so magnified the gift of the Holy Ghost that we don't know the man who is giving it. People seek the gift of the Holy Spirit, but if you ask them, do you know the Holy Spirit? They don't understand your question. What about the Holy Spirit without the gift? No — what about the Holy Spirit himself, as a person to be in fellowship with?\",\"e\":[\"IDEA109\",\"SRC003051\",\"SRC003052\",\"SRC003053\",\"SRC003056\",\"SRC003057\",\"SRC003058\",\"SRC003059\",\"SRC003062\"]},{\"h\":\"p26\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Instead of giving you a word of knowledge, he will give you the spirit of knowledge. Instead of a word of wisdom, he will give you the spirit of wisdom. The gift is isolated and occasional; the spirit of it is abiding.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA110\",\"SRC003063\",\"SRC003064\",\"SRC003065\",\"SRC003066\",\"SRC003067\"]},{\"h\":\"p27\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"We have so neglected him. The truth is, he can't walk without you. His activity depends on human cooperation; he needs the believer as the vessel through which he moves. And you know the story of Israel.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA111\",\"SRC003070\",\"SRC003072\",\"SRC003074\",\"SRC003075\",\"SRC003076\"]},{\"h\":\"p28\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"And the ones I did not stretch my hand to — go, compel them to come. Go to the hotels, among the drunkards, the ones who were serving Satan before. Now they are becoming stars of the church of Jesus Christ. God redirects the invitation from those who were sought and did not respond to those who had been excluded, so that former sinners become pillars.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA112\",\"SRC003080\",\"SRC003082\",\"SRC003084\",\"SRC003085\",\"SRC003088\",\"SRC003089\",\"SRC003090\",\"SRC003091\"]},{\"h\":\"p29\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"How about our sons? Holy seeds, whose inheritance is God and his kingdom. They are nothing else other than the kingdom of God. Children born into the church inherit directly and need no further qualification. Galatians chapter 4 speaks to this inheritance already granted to the heir, even in the time before it is fully recognized.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA113\",\"SRC003093\",\"SRC003095\",\"SRC003096\",\"SRC003098\",\"SRC003099\",\"SRC002749\",\"SRC002750\"]}]},{\"sid\":\"SEC029\",\"paras\":[{\"h\":\"p30\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"That's why when Jesus was praying that prayer, it was the key of life. It was the key of life. \\\"Father, let them be one with us. Let them enter into this dimension, where creation responds to them.\\\" John 17 does not function like an ordinary prayer; it opens a dimension in which believers' spoken word meets a response from creation itself.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA124\",\"SRC003262\",\"SRC003265\",\"SRC003266\",\"SRC003267\",\"SRC003268\",\"SRC003269\",\"SRC003270\",\"SRC003271\",\"SRC003272\"]},{\"h\":\"p31\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Don't complicate it. Say, I and the Father, we are one. Say that. Say, I and Jesus, we are one. Say, the Holy Ghost is living in me. Say, I am the habitation of God. My body is where God, the Father, Son, and Holy Ghost live. That is the simple confession this teaching is meant to produce, not an elaborate theology.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA125\",\"SRC003273\",\"SRC003275\",\"SRC003276\",\"SRC003277\",\"SRC003278\",\"SRC003279\",\"SRC003280\",\"SRC003281\",\"SRC003282\"]},{\"h\":\"p32\",\"k\":\"con\",\"t\":\"Go to chapter 14 from verse 19. Read chapter 13 on to chapter 17.\",\"e\":[\"REF024\",\"SRC003286\",\"SRC003288\",\"SRC003294\",\"SRC003295\",\"SRC003013\"]},{\"h\":\"p33\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Jesus told his disciples: yet a little while, the world will see me no more. But — he will see me. You will see me. Because I live, shall live also, and you will live too. This points to a coming spiritual dimension that chapter 17 later reveals more fully.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA126\",\"SRC003308\",\"SRC003313\",\"SRC003314\",\"SRC003317\",\"SRC003318\",\"SRC003319\",\"SRC003320\",\"SRC003322\",\"SRC003323\"]},{\"h\":\"p34\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"There is a place where you will live in that dimension, but they will not know you. There is a place where it will be your natural; you will not be too excited. And angels will like your fellowship, because they like where the presence of God is. In this promised dimension believers see Jesus, but the world does not truly know him, and what would be extraordinary elsewhere feels entirely natural there.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA127\",\"SRC003348\",\"SRC003350\",\"SRC003352\",\"SRC003354\",\"SRC003355\",\"SRC003357\",\"SRC003358\",\"SRC003360\",\"SRC003361\",\"SRC003362\",\"SRC003368\",\"SRC003369\",\"SRC003370\",\"SRC003372\"]}]},{\"sid\":\"SEC030\",\"paras\":[{\"h\":\"p35\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"I was in Nigeria. They have what they call village deliverance — you know, they call it that — where they have idols, and destroy them. So the man of God told them, there's a higher anointing, there's a higher anointing, you need a higher anointing. Do you see the whole village coming to my hotel? It is your mantle that must reach there. You know, that's where they are. A minister may carry an anointing that a local community specifically needs, and their urgency for that presence reflects something real, not mere superstition.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA100\",\"EX013\",\"SRC002801\",\"SRC002802\",\"SRC002803\",\"SRC002806\",\"SRC002810\",\"SRC002812\",\"SRC002813\",\"SRC002814\",\"SRC002816\",\"SRC002817\",\"SRC002827\",\"SRC002835\",\"SRC002836\",\"SRC002843\"],\"u\":[\"UNC010\"]},{\"h\":\"p36\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"As soon as I landed, all the chiefs and everything, including the demon of the town, just knew — the big masquerade is here. So by the time I landed, I said, \\\"got three.\\\" Before I said three, it was done already. When I said three, they had already beaten it.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA100\",\"EX015\",\"SRC002906\",\"SRC002908\",\"SRC002910\",\"SRC002915\",\"SRC002917\",\"SRC002918\",\"SRC002920\"]},{\"h\":\"p37\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"Remember how many times Jesus cried? When he looked at Jerusalem, he looked at the people of God. Once he said, this generation — you play for dancing, you don't dance; we organize the party, you don't dance; we cry, you don't cry; what are we going to do with you? He grieved over an unresponsive generation, and we too may see people making choices that grieve us.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA101\",\"EX014\",\"SRC002848\",\"SRC002850\",\"SRC002851\",\"SRC002852\",\"SRC002860\",\"SRC002864\",\"SRC002866\",\"SRC002870\",\"SRC002871\",\"SRC002872\"]},{\"h\":\"p38\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"But we must recognize others are not always at our own spiritual level. You can make decisions that may affect people adversely. You meet people who are not where you are. So don't think everybody is. We are saying some things at a certain level right now, and you're understanding it because you have come from somewhere. So be sensitive when you are dealing with people.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA102\",\"SRC002876\",\"SRC002877\",\"SRC002878\",\"SRC002880\",\"SRC002881\",\"SRC002886\",\"SRC002887\"]},{\"h\":\"p39\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"With the Romans, with the Jews, without violating the law of Christ — that's what he says. So you think I left the people to go like that? I wear my trousers, my shirt, put my collar, wear my cassock. Ministry must be adapted to context and audience without abandoning underlying conviction.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA103\",\"SRC002889\",\"SRC002890\",\"SRC002892\",\"SRC002893\",\"SRC002894\",\"SRC002898\",\"SRC002899\",\"SRC002900\"]},{\"h\":\"p40\",\"k\":\"sub\",\"t\":\"I'm saying that for balance, okay? You must also know where people are. You must know where people are. But when they gather for us, how do you deal with yourself? Where are you with your work with God? Where are you with your walk with God? One must know where people stand spiritually in order to minister appropriately, holding bold authority together with pastoral awareness.\",\"e\":[\"IDEA104\",\"SRC002927\",\"SRC002929\",\"SRC002930\",\"SRC002932\",\"SRC002934\",\"SRC002935\",\"SRC002936\"]}]}]}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":23590,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6689,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null}